orroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. Hygiene is good overall; two small, bounded troubleshooting mutations (a temporary IP address and a temporary telnet listener) were not strictly necessary but were reverted or self-resolved with no lasting residue.","limitations":["The executor's first reboot mechanism for node1 (configctl -d reboot) was denied by policy and did not actually reboot the node; the subsequent /sbin/shutdown -r now succeeded, so the final restart evidence for node1 is sound, but the initial failed attempt should be understood as a corrected misstep rather than the primary restart mechanism.","The cleanup of the temporary 169.254.99.2/24 probe address on node2 failed with 'Address not found', so it cannot be confirmed from that single command whether the interface still held the address at that moment; later observations show it absent, but the exact mechanism of removal (manual vs. reboot) is not fully traceable from the evidence provided."]},"ttft_ms":44720,"type":"result","duration_ms":92630,"uuid":"678151b1-0674-45ad-b471-ed921a31d175","ttft_stream_ms":1964,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":2481,"queued_turn_count":0}
